Identified configuration error and daemon startup failure

Two issues: rotate-interval: 1day is invalid syntax in Suricata 4.1.10 — needs integer seconds. And -D daemonize isn't holding. Fix both:
sh

# Fix rotate-interval - replace with seconds integer
sed -i 's/rotate-interval: 1day/rotate-interval: 86400/' /opt/etc/suricata/suricata.yaml

# Verify fix
grep "rotate-interval" /opt/etc/suricata/suricata.yaml

Fix the init script daemonize — 4.1.10 uses --daemon not -D:
sh

sed -i 's/$SURICATA -c $CONFIG --af-packet --pidfile $PIDFILE -D/$SURICATA -c $CONFIG --af-packet --pidfile $PIDFILE --daemon/' /opt/etc/init.d/S50suricata

Then test and start:
sh

# Validate
/opt/bin/suricata -c /opt/etc/suricata/suricata.yaml --af-packet -T

# Start
/opt/etc/init.d/S50suricata start
sleep 8
/opt/etc/init.d/S50suricata status

# Watch startup
