Apr 13
Determined that tls_state cannot be created as variable; upgrade or modify rules instead

Straight answer: can't be done. tls_state is a C-level engine keyword compiled into Suricata 5.x — it's not a yaml variable, it's a pattern matching primitive that doesn't exist in the 4.1.10 binary at all. No amount of yaml config creates it.

Two real options:

Option 1 — Upgrade Suricata via entware:
sh

/opt/bin/opkg update
/opt/bin/opkg list | grep suricata

If entware has 5.x or 6.x available that's the clean fix — all 54 ET rule files load without modification.

Option 2 — Strip the incompatible keywords from rules so 4.1.10 loads them:
sh

# Count how many rules use tls_state
grep -c "tls_state" /opt/etc/suricata/rules/emerging-trojan.rules

# Strip tls_state rules from all rule files
for f in /opt/etc/suricata/rules/*.rules; do
    sed -i '/tls_state/d' "$f"
done

# Also strip other 5.x keywords that will fail
for f in /opt/etc/suricata/rules/*.rules; do
    sed -i '/ja3\.string\|ja3s\|hassh\|http\.request_line/d' "$f"
done

# Then restore full rule-files list and test
/opt/bin/suricata -c /opt/etc/suricata/suricata.yaml --af-packet -T

Check entware first — upgrading is cleaner than stripping rules. Paste the opkg list | grep suricata output.

