Apr 13
Diagnosed benign warnings stemming from incomplete cross-file dependencies

Those are not errors — they're benign cross-file dependency warnings. A flowbit works in two stages: one rule sets it when it sees stage 1 of an attack, another rule checks it when it sees stage 2. The warnings mean the setter rules live in rule files we didn't load, so the checker rules are orphaned.

The engine is running clean — PID 13719, no errors. These warnings don't break anything, they just mean some multi-stage detection chains are incomplete.

Fix is simple — load all 54 rule files since we're on 7.0.14 with enough RAM:
sh

# Generate rule-files list from everything in the rules directory
ls /opt/etc/suricata/rules/*.rules | sed 's|/opt/etc/suricata/rules/||' | sed 's/^/  - /'

Then replace the rule-files section in the yaml with the full list:
sh

# Remove existing rule-files block
sed -i '/^rule-files:/,/^[^ ]/{ /^rule-files:/d; /^  - /d }' /opt/etc/suricata/suricata.yaml

# Append full ruleset
echo "rule-files:" >> /opt/etc/suricata/suricata.yaml
ls /opt/etc/suricata/rules/*.rules | sed 's|/opt/etc/suricata/rules/||' | sed 's/^/  - /' >> /opt/etc/suricata/suricata.yaml

# Validate
/opt/bin/suricata -c /opt/etc/suricata/suricata.yaml --af-packet -T

# Restart with full ruleset
/opt/etc/init.d/S50suricata stop
sleep 3
rm -f /opt/var/run/suricata.pid
/opt/etc/init.d/S50suricata start
sleep 15
/opt/etc/init.d/S50suricata status
tail -5 /opt/var/log/suricata/suricata.log

Expect startup to take longer with all 54 files loading — that's normal.

